-- =========================================================================
-- AI — the `AI` CAPABILITY, authored as a Fenel record-of-methods type
-- (module-substrate Phase 3l: "typeclasses ARE types" carbon-copy of email's
-- `capability.fenel`, no TS `ClassSeed` const).
--
-- A capability is a record whose fields are its methods (each an arrow type) —
-- the same shape `fenel/std/algebra.fenel` declares Functor/Monad/Monoid. The
-- ai seam reads this type and `seedFromType`s it into the dispatch `ClassSeed`
-- (replacing the retired hand-written const). `AI` is NOMINAL — it is
-- dispatched by PROVIDER NAME via `resolveCapabilityMethod` (which splits a
-- qualified `AI.<method>` action and picks the highest-priority provider
-- instance), NOT by `seedFromType`'s effect-dispatch arg-position path; the
-- method carries no class type-param in argument position. So the derived seed
-- needs only the right method NAME + signature (`complete`).
--
-- The single method `complete` is a PLAIN IDENT — no dotted-name wrinkle
-- (email's `domain.*` faux-namespace rename is not needed here). Its arrow
-- mirrors the retired TS method: prompt String -> outputSchema {} -> system
-- String -> config {} -> {}. The two `{}` placeholders ride along verbatim
-- (parity; the documented anti-pattern, not "fixed" here).
--
-- This file is loaded SEPARATELY from `ai.fenel` (NOT merged) so the `AI`
-- capability type does NOT enter `aiModule.entities` (the 2-data-type roster);
-- the seam reads only its type to derive the seed. The capability NAME is
-- `AI` (kept byte-identical to the retired const).
-- =========================================================================

AI = AI complete: (String -> {} -> String -> {} -> {})
